Whilst I may not agree with everything that Grant Gustafson has suggested
in re floats and LaTeX, I do feel that his heart is in the right place;
however, he has, I believe, omitted a most important desideratum: that
of placing a float so that it is visible from its point of reference,
\stress {even if that means placing the figure on the page _preceding_
the point of reference}.  Which is a verbose way of saying that LaTeX
should take the spread as its basic element of layout rather than the page,
at least for `book'-like document classes.

					Philip Taylor, RHBNC.

